TH02 MAIN: bomb_bft_8tiles_put_8() loop compares a signed counter.

The original MAIN.EXE ends the 8-tile loop with `cmp si, 8 / jl` (7C) at
program offset 0xEEBB. Borland's `_SI` pseudo-register is unsigned, so
ReC98's `while(_SI < BYTE_DOTS)` compiles to `jb` (72). Casting to int makes
TCC 4.02 emit `jl`; with it every ReC98 C/C++ contribution in MAIN.EXE is
byte-equal. Found by scripts/rec98_th02_ledger.py.

diff --git a/th02/main/player/bomb.cpp b/th02/main/player/bomb.cpp
index 44b8f433..8c925ff1 100644
--- a/th02/main/player/bomb.cpp
+++ b/th02/main/player/bomb.cpp
@@ -229,7 +229,7 @@ void pascal near bomb_bft_8tiles_put_8(
 		tile_cur >>= 1;
 		_DI += TILE_VRAM_W;
 		_SI++;
-	} while(_SI < BYTE_DOTS);
+	} while(static_cast<int>(_SI) < BYTE_DOTS);
 
 	#undef tiles
 	#undef tile_cur
